# === .NET ===
bin/
obj/
*.user
*.suo
.vs/
*.dotCover
*.dbmdl

# === Node / TypeScript / Vite ===
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
*.tsbuildinfo

# Vite build output for the backoffice extension is generated (research.md §2) - the source of
# truth is Client/src, not the compiled bundle.
src/UmbracoMediaAudit/wwwroot/App_Plugins/

# === Umbraco runtime/dev data (sample site) ===
# Local SQLite dev database, Lucene/NuCache indexes, logs, and uploaded media are all generated by
# running the sample site (src/UmbracoMediaAudit.Web) locally - never source-controlled.
src/UmbracoMediaAudit.Web/umbraco/Data/
src/UmbracoMediaAudit.Web/umbraco/Logs/
src/UmbracoMediaAudit.Web/wwwroot/media/
src/UmbracoMediaAudit.Web/wwwroot/umbraco/

# uSync (src/UmbracoMediaAudit.Web/uSync/) exports schema-as-code on every startup - see its own
# README.md. DataTypes/ContentTypes/MemberTypes/Languages/MediaTypes/RelationTypes are genuinely
# reproducible schema and ARE committed. Its "Media" folder just tracks node metadata (name/path/
# dates) for whatever's currently uploaded in wwwroot/media/ - since that folder is itself
# gitignored above, committing Media/ configs would reference files that don't exist on a fresh
# clone, so it's excluded the same way.
src/UmbracoMediaAudit.Web/uSync/v*/Media/

# === OS / editor cruft ===
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
.idea/
